# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and local configuration -- NEVER commit these.
# Spec section 33: no API key, database credential, JWT secret, service
# credential, push token or private key is hardcoded or committed to Git.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The one deliberate exception, added 2026-08-23 with phase 16.1. It holds the
# production API origin and nothing else. Vite inlines every VITE_-prefixed
# value into the public bundle, so anything in that file is served to every
# visitor whether or not it is committed here - keeping it out would hide it
# from developers and from nobody else, while letting an unset variable fall
# back to localhost in a build nobody would notice was broken.
# `.env.native` joined it on 2026-08-31 for the same reason and with the same
# guard. It holds the API origin and the client flag, both of which are inlined
# into a bundle that ships inside an APK - a file anybody can unzip.
!frontend/.env.production
!frontend/.env.native

application-local.properties
application-local.yml
application-local.yaml
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.jks
*.keystore
service-account*.json
google-services.json
GoogleService-Info.plist

